  "scenarios": [
    "Independent world_change match/into schema, enabled world definitions, native partial-state matching, invalid/unsupported references and candidate validation without changing the live registry.",
    "Native/custom block conversions in both directions, explicit air, same-ID replacement, helper ownership, server API calls and protected furnishing replacements.",
    "Replacement/custom/native protection cancellation, block source/destination permissions, furnishing use/interaction suffixes, adventure-mode furnishing state/footprint changes, native footprint veto, exact source callback replacement, guarded reentry and reload refusal while committing.",
    "A native break attempted from placement preparation is denied; logical ownership survives consistency queries during the temporary backing write.",
    "Native container rollback retains three diamonds and tile PDC without spilled duplicates; committed conversion releases its stored contents once on all four endpoints.",
    "Actual furnace cooking creates a stored recipe count; placement veto retains it without XP leakage; committed replacement releases the smelted item and exactly one XP.",
    "Supported-crop veto/preparation rollback and growth-lock release, then committed support removal; indexed custom lava cannot be changed through a vanilla selector.",
    "Occupied beehive type changes preserve the source by rejection; same-material state changes retain the bee. Cross-material entity migration is not implemented.",
    "Forced one-shot native tracking failure restores the original ID/backing/helper; native main/offhand/furnishing inputs, delayed held source replacement, physical self-change, retired-anchor recreation and reload persistence.",
    "Furnishing collision removal tolerates a spawn observer querying the pending source; final anchor/footprint state is validated before completion.",
    "Paper 26.3 emits a temporary native container drop that triggers a nested upper-cell replacement. That nested committed payload escapes the outer escrow exactly once. Other endpoints did not emit that temporary drop and do not claim this additional native path."
  ],
  "development_findings": [
    "Initial new-candidate checks exposed ordinary consistency reconciliation retiring a logically owned source during its temporary backing write. Committing block/furnishing scopes now retain logical identity while explicit raw-state checks guard publication.",
    "Physical action getters initially rejected their own temporary backing change, including recreation from a retired empty anchor. A separate resident ownership authority now survives only the owned transaction.",
    "Paper can emit native container contents during a temporary type change that is later cancelled. Original native payload snapshots and scoped item/XP escrow prevent rollback duplication and cross-fork payload loss.",
    "Nested committed payload release is excluded from enclosing write escrow. Stored furnace XP uses the public recipe state, native float multiplication and ordinary fractional rounding.",
    "Earlier failed development assertions overlap and are not separate bug counts. Only the accepted terminal runs above contribute to the totals."
  ],
  "fixture_corrections": [
    "Native chest/beehive fixture snapshots are updated explicitly before source-state assertions; changing a captured snapshot does not automatically update its live block.",
    "The longer furnace-cooking scenario enables allow-flight only on its isolated verification servers to avoid a floating-client disconnect during the native tick wait. Production player/game-mode restrictions were not weakened.",
    "Native-break attempts additionally check unchanged candidate backing and retained logical identity rather than relying only on a helper return value.",
    "Native XP observations retain unique entity UUIDs, so multiple spawn notifications for one orb do not inflate the awarded amount."
